#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0092 expect=violation domain=SE
#note "SEUPDES column absent while row 2 codes ETCD='UNPLAN'. Requirements.Variables.All [ETCD, SEUPDES] now gates the rule out -> auditable skip naming the column instead of a violation carried by the bare empty(SEUPDES) leaf (absent = all-missing, EC-43). Verdict 2-1 (T1-37): the absence is itself reportable, and the minted sister PMDA-SD9723 reports it ONCE for this dataset. SUPERSEDES the 2026-08-27 rationale for REMOVING the gate ('no rule anywhere reports its absence') - the sister is exactly that rule, which is what the removal was missing."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN   | 2020-01-01
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | UNPLAN | 2020-01-10
